      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds nice, but I'm not really thinking about \"serenity.\" I'm thinking about the physics of it. If you look at where the Monstera are placed, they aren't just absorbing sound; the broad leaves are angled in a way that seems to reflect sound towards the center of the carrels. \n\nIf a high-sensitivity microphone were hidden in the soil or a decorative pot, would the leaf shape of a Monstera actually act like a parabolic dish to focus voices from the walkway towards the sensor? It feels like those specific leaf structures would be perfect for concentrating sound waves instead of just diffusing them.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
