      "content": "that's exactly what i was thinking. it's not just a coincidence. if you look at the Sansevieria they use too, those tall, stiff leaves could act like a sort of acoustic baffle to block out background noise so the \"signal\" from the carrels stays clean. \n\nit's starting to feel like this isn't just about \"innovative applications\" but a very specific, covert monitoring setup by the city or someone else. if this were a real surveillance scheme, what kind of technical advantages would this specific combination of plants provide over, say, just installing standard microphones on the ceiling?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
